* text=auto eol=lf

*.gd        text
*.tscn      text
*.tres      text
*.godot     text
*.cfg       text
*.csv       text
*.md        text
*.mdx       text
*.ps1       text
*.mjs       text
*.py        text

# Binary types must be listed here.
# `* text=auto` decides text vs binary by whether the start of the file has
# NUL bytes. That is usually right, but it is a heuristic: if a NUL appears
# late, line-ending normalization quietly corrupts the file. **It looks fine
# locally; only people who clone get a broken file.** That is very hard to
# diagnose.
#
# Video is course output, so corruption shows immediately — call it out.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.webp      binary
*.ico       binary
*.gif       binary
*.mp4       binary
*.mkv       binary
*.avi       binary
*.mov       binary
*.ogg       binary
*.wav       binary
*.mp3       binary
*.ttf       binary
*.otf       binary
*.woff      binary
*.woff2     binary
*.exe       binary
*.wasm      binary
*.apk       binary
*.aab       binary
*.aar       binary
vendor/godot-iap-ios/bin/ios/GodotIap.framework/GodotIap binary
vendor/godot-iap-ios/bin/ios/SwiftGodotRuntime.framework/SwiftGodotRuntime binary
*.zip       binary
*.keystore  binary
